  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Frost/Freeze late tonight into early Sunday \nmorning \n\n930 PM Update...\nWe took a couple degs off the normally cold spots for \novernight. BFD, SEG and THV are doing what they do...dropping \nfast. It's real. They just radiate efficiently and get a cold \npool in their respective local low spots. This makes it easier \nto justify - and perhaps verify - the freeze warning. We shall\nsee by 8 AM. \n\nPrevious...\nBands of north-south oriented clouds off of the Great Lakes \ncontinue to decrease in coverage this afternoon as high pressure\nbuilds into the region from the west. This high will set up \nfavorable conditions for a widespread frost/freeze tonight into \nearly Sunday morning. Low temperatures will be in the 25-30 \ndegree range for much of the region tonight and a Freeze Warning\nremains in effect for all zones except for McKean County where \nthe growing season has already ended. The overnight frost/freeze\nrisk will continue for portions of CPA into next week, but \nadditional headline issuances will depend on where the growing \nseason remains active after tonight's freeze.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Extended stretch of dry weather next week\n\nHigh pressure anchored on the northwest side of a Nor'easter\ndeveloping along a stalled front off of the NC coast will \nprovide another extended stretch of dry weather in CPA Sunday \nthrough next week. There is still considerable uncertainty\nregarding how close the Nor'easter tracks to the coast, but the\nvast majority of model solutions keep and precip associated \nwith the storm off to our east. This pattern will feature \nseasonably warm days, chilly nights, and low humidity.",
